From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: muffin-os <muffin-os@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 3 Nov 2026 11:40:12 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] add muffin target

Add `target_os = "muffin"` for the muffin-os userspace. The values
mirror `kernel/abi` in muffin-os/muffin: errno numbers, `O_*`, `AT_*`,
`F_*`, `POSIX_FADV_*`, `SEEK_*`, `CLOCK_*`, `SIG*`, `SA_*`, `SIG_*`,
`PROT_*`, `MAP_*` and `PATH_MAX`. `S_IF*` and the permission bits are
the POSIX octal values, because the kernel has no file mode yet.

The wait status macros follow the kernel encoding, "exit code, or
128 + signo" (`kernel/syscall/src/access/process.rs`). Nothing stops or
continues, so `WIFSTOPPED` and `WIFCONTINUED` are always false.

The module mirrors NuttX in shape. NuttX also:
- links no system library in `src/unix/mod.rs`; muffin does the same
  because `muffinos-rt` is a Rust rlib that std links directly.
- provides a `src/new/<os>/unistd.rs`; the unix family export in
  `src/new/mod.rs` requires it.
The NuttX exclusions for `locale_t` and `ipv6_mreq` are not mirrored;
muffin keeps the shared definitions.

Only `sockaddr` and `addrinfo` exist among the socket types, because
the shared externs declare `connect` and `getaddrinfo` against them.
The kernel has no socket syscall, so the other socket types are
omitted until it does.

